caregivers are ordinary family members  who are stepping forward to look after  their loved ones who have to deal with  various health conditions and needs my  name is Lakshmi  I'm a designer at fuel for we look at  interactions that ordinary people have  with care systems and redesign them it  was 2016 the National Council of Social  Service Singapore came calling  Singapore's caregiving landscape needed  a new approach due to the complexities  of the experience changing demographics  changing families aging population as  well as the maze of assistance to  navigate across media caregiving  experience very lonely and stressful we  conducted design ethnography following  the day two days of 10 different  caregivers experiencing the world from  their perspective  we then synthesize their unique journeys  to create a common framework looking at  the experience of caregiving as a series  of emotional highs and lows seeing  caregiving through this lens opened up  opportunities we knew we could design  specific solutions that will directly  support caregivers at various points and  across the system as a whole  a few topologies emerged we found out  that each caregiver was different and  had different issues and needs it was  important to create different caregiver  technologies because we knew who they  were and what they needed exactly and it  put them at the very center of the  design process we discovered caregivers  are the red thread that connects the  social and healthcare landscape and it  is they that journey with their loved  ones across social and healthcare  services and that's when it clipped the  impact on health and social care as we  know it would be infinitely better if  caregivers were properly supported a  design workshop was held designers  created initial ideas based on insight  then other disciplines came in and  iterated these ideas and added their own  ideas everyone working together until we  got this we designed a physical space  where caregivers can receive support  meet fellow caregivers and attend  coaching programs and a virtual space  that would make it easy for caregivers  to connect and link up with parties and  organizations and sectors online plus a  new role the family manager and the we  care toolkit a practical guide for  social workers  this was a design project but it wasn't  done just by designers we had  researchers social workers health care  workers filmmakers and leaders from  across sectors we even recruited the  caregivers the roles started to blur we  work well together because we had one  unifying purpose research was important  but the end goal is the actioning of the  insights and making it a reality our  ideas were integrated into their  enabling master plan for Singapore this  project has shown the potential of  design and how it can impact society we  want to say that we have found the  answer to caregiving but this is just  the beginning the beginning to  normalizing caregiving as well as  building a compassionate community  through design  you  [Music]  [Music]
 

